KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 4 --no-unwinding-assertions --object-bits 10
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member-template ctor reconstructing the class pack has its body instantiated: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^.*dereference failure: pointer NULL in this->invoker.*$
^.*no body for callee.*$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
KNOWNBUG ([temp.variadic] + [temp.mem]): a member function template of a class
template partial-specialized on a function type R(Args...) whose body uses the
enclosing class's parameter pack Args... to form a template argument (e.g.
reconstructing R(Args...) to instantiate another template) is left with an
uninstantiated (empty) body.  This is std::function's converting constructor
  typedef _Function_handler<_Res(_ArgTypes...), _Functor> _Handler;
  _M_invoker = &_Handler::_M_invoke;
so _M_invoker is never assigned and std::function calls dereference a null
function pointer.  Reclassify CORE once the member template body is
instantiated.
